00:15:19.350 --> 00:15:22.150
So it's, you know, as accurate as step counts are.

00:15:22.150 --> 00:15:25.760
There's a, but, so it took me.

00:15:25.760 --> 00:15:27.840
So the PCT, quick stats here.

00:15:29.090 --> 00:15:30.610
PCT is broken into five sections,

00:15:30.610 --> 00:15:32.770
the desert, the Sierra, North and California,

00:15:32.770 --> 00:15:33.730
Oregon and Washington.

00:15:34.610 --> 00:15:39.010
It took me 40 days to get from the desert

00:15:39.010 --> 00:15:40.130
to the beginning of the Sierra.

00:15:41.360 --> 00:15:44.680
I took four, what's called a zero day in there

00:15:44.680 --> 00:15:45.960
or a day I don't do any miles.

00:15:45.960 --> 00:15:47.960
I took three days off to hang with some friends

00:15:47.960 --> 00:15:51.560
in near Wrightwood and I took one day off

00:15:51.560 --> 00:15:56.280
in Tehachapi, so about 700 miles average

00:15:56.280 --> 00:15:58.440
for the days I hiked just under 20 miles a day.

00:15:59.270 --> 00:16:00.550
Not too much elevation game,

00:16:00.630 --> 00:16:02.470
but you'll see as I go through this stuff,

00:16:02.470 --> 00:16:03.510
which is only interesting to me,

00:16:03.510 --> 00:16:04.870
but you can ask questions is,

00:16:06.950 --> 00:16:08.550
you know, average miles in the desert,

00:16:08.550 --> 00:16:11.910
19 and a half median, just under 19 and a half.

00:16:11.910 --> 00:16:14.470
And my biggest days, I had two 27 mile days.

00:16:14.470 --> 00:16:17.270
My longest hiking day in the desert was 27.8 miles.

00:16:17.910 --> 00:16:19.590
So I'm warmed up, I'm warmed up.

00:16:19.590 --> 00:16:20.630
I've gotten to the mountains.

00:16:20.630 --> 00:16:21.990
They're steep, there's snow.

00:16:22.710 --> 00:16:24.550
Did I slow down a little?

00:16:25.110 --> 00:16:28.870
Took me 22 days to get from Kennedy Meadows

00:16:28.870 --> 00:16:31.430
to Sonora Pass or what we call Kennedy Meadows South

00:16:31.430 --> 00:16:32.870
and Kennedy Meadows North.

00:16:32.870 --> 00:16:34.390
It's funny, there's a Kennedy Meadows South

00:16:34.390 --> 00:16:35.510
and Kennedy Meadows North.

00:16:35.510 --> 00:16:37.430
They're named for two different Kennedys

00:16:37.430 --> 00:16:38.870
and they happen to just be on both sides

00:16:38.870 --> 00:16:40.550
of the Sierra Range.

00:16:40.550 --> 00:16:41.590
PCT is weird.

00:16:41.590 --> 00:16:43.990
I took three, did I take three zero days in there?

00:16:43.990 --> 00:16:44.790
Where did I zero?

00:16:46.000 --> 00:16:47.600
My stats say I took three zero days.

00:16:47.600 --> 00:16:51.360
I took one in, oh no,

00:16:51.360 --> 00:16:52.480
I don't remember where I took them off.

00:16:52.480 --> 00:16:53.360
Look at my sheet.

00:16:53.360 --> 00:16:54.000
I should remember.

00:16:54.000 --> 00:16:59.380
I know I took one in Lake Tahoe.

00:17:00.630 --> 00:17:01.670
Where were the other two?

00:17:01.670 --> 00:17:02.230
Oh, you know what?

00:17:02.230 --> 00:17:04.790
I took two zero, a zero and a half in Kennedy Meadows.

00:17:04.790 --> 00:17:07.160
I counted as zero days.

00:17:08.790 --> 00:17:10.230
That section's not that long.

00:17:10.230 --> 00:17:11.670
Average 17 miles a day.

00:17:11.670 --> 00:17:13.910
But did do, it's a lot of snow,

00:17:13.910 --> 00:17:15.910
a lot of water crossing, a lot of up and down.

00:17:15.910 --> 00:17:17.430
Did get a 25 mile day in there.

00:17:17.990 --> 00:17:18.710
No big deal.

00:17:18.710 --> 00:17:19.590
Pack was heavier too.

00:17:20.530 --> 00:17:22.370
Northern California, also known as hell,

00:17:22.930 --> 00:17:24.450
which is from Kennedy Meadows North

00:17:24.450 --> 00:17:25.490
up to the Oregon border.

00:17:26.770 --> 00:17:29.650
As I mentioned before, it's dry and desert

00:17:29.650 --> 00:17:32.450
and ash and climbing over trees all the time

00:17:32.450 --> 00:17:34.290
because the trail's not that one that will maintain.

00:17:36.210 --> 00:17:38.610
35 days, two zeros, one in Shasta.

00:17:38.610 --> 00:17:39.490
Small interruption.

00:17:41.250 --> 00:17:43.090
At which day did you get your name?

00:17:44.470 --> 00:17:47.110
Oh, I don't know which day in the desert.

00:17:48.150 --> 00:17:49.190
And we're going to come back to this.

00:17:49.190 --> 00:17:50.630
So in the desert, I think I don't know

00:17:50.630 --> 00:17:51.910
if I've told this story.

00:17:51.910 --> 00:17:54.710
So I kept a trail journal and I blogged

00:17:54.710 --> 00:17:56.150
a little bit from my trail journal

00:17:56.150 --> 00:17:58.070
